TI  - Psilocybin increases brain network integration in patients with depression
T2  - NATURE MEDICINE
M3  - Editorial Material
AB  - Clinical trial results show that psilocybin, a potent psychedelic, has antidepressant effects in patients with depression and is more effective than escitalopram. Functional MRI experiments revealed a decrease in brain modularity after psilocybin therapy, indicative of an increase in the global integration of the brain's functional networks.
