AU  - Weissman, Cory R.
TI  - The effect of psilocybin on empathy and prosocial behavior: a proposed mechanism for enduring antidepressant effects
T2  - NPJ MENTAL HEALTH RESEARCH
M3  - Review
AB  - Psilocybin is a serotonergic psychedelic shown to have enduring antidepressant effects. Currently, the mechanism for its enduring effects is not well understood. Empathy and prosocial behavior may be important for understanding the therapeutic benefit of psilocybin. In this article we review the effect of psilocybin on empathy and prosocial behavior. Moreover, we propose that psilocybin may induce a positive feedback loop involving empathy and prosocial behavior which helps explain the observed, enduring antidepressant effects.
