TI  - Exploring the Role of Psychedelics in Modulating Ego and Treating Neuropsychiatric Disorders
T2  - ACS CHEMICAL NEUROSCIENCE
M3  - Editorial Material
AB  - This viewpoint explores the therapeutic potential of psychedelics in treating neuropsychiatric disorders, particularly through the modulation of brain entropy and the experience of ego dissolution. Psychedelics disrupt rigid neural patterns, facilitating enhanced connectivity and fostering profound emotional breakthroughs that may alleviate symptoms of disorders like depression, anxiety, PTSD, and addiction. Despite their promising potential, the clinical application of psychedelics presents significant challenges, including the need for careful patient screening, managing adverse experiences, and addressing ethical considerations, all of which are essential for their safe integration into therapy.
